    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3bb47b3_aa22d3fc",
        "filename": "common/ec_ec_comm_master.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-04T03:10:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it makes much sense the pad the packets to 32-bit boundaries, now that we use a crc8 instead of crc32 (we\u0027d have to pad every packet with 3 bytes, that seems wasteful...)\n\nI\u0027m sadly aware of the space issue, thankfully this isn\u0027t a problem yet. I updated the comment a bit, I think it\u0027s possible to change the function API to fix this, but I\u0027d rather move forward with this limitation, for now.",
